--- !u!114 &2065145610
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2065145608}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4afc7b58bd1eec149a28b8db4ceec237, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GuideController
  topicsMenuPanel: {fileID: 1755571256}
  topicViewPanel: {fileID: 246410209}
  topicButtonDiagnosis: {fileID: 1007304155}
  topicButtonBlackMarket: {fileID: 1500974441}
  topicButtonLab: {fileID: 213038913}
  topicButtonExternalVirus: {fileID: 500539417}
  topicButtonSecretary: {fileID: 375968259}
  topicButtonEndings: {fileID: 512386580}
  backButton: {fileID: 1939183045}
  topicTitleText: {fileID: 570995396}
  topicBodyText: {fileID: 960906683}
  closeButton: {fileID: 1353797971}
  topicDiagnosis:
    topicName: Patient Diagnosis
    topicBody: 'Patients come to you with symptoms they don''t fully understand.
      Talk to them, listen carefully, and read between the lines - what they say
      (and how they say it) tells you who they are.

      The computer in the <b>Laboratory</b>
      helps you keep track of what you''ve learned about each one. The more you know
      them, the easier it becomes to recognize what''s wrong.

      Get the diagnosis
      right and <b>trust</b> grows. Get it wrong and the patient leaves still sick
      and a little less convinced you know what you''re doing.

      Each session
      last for 3 minutes. Try to select the diagnosis in the <b>Notebook</b> and
      gather as much information as possible about the patient before the time expires.

      Each
      information about the patient is revealed in their personal <b>Record</b> once
      they mention it during a conversation. '
  topicBlackMarket:
    topicName: Black Market
    topicBody: 'The Black Market is where you can buy <b>Symptoms</b> to either create
      your own virus or make a cure to fight an Unkown Virus (event).

      If you
      go to the Shop, you are able to only purchase 3 symptoms "daily". Symptoms
      in the shop refresh daily, but they won''t appear again once you buy them,
      at least until they are used.

      That''s also the place where you can start
      spreading your own "completed virus" at a cost of 100 coins, by talking to
      the Spreader.'
  topicLab:
    topicName: Laboratory
    topicBody: 'The Laboratory is where you can make things happen.

      That''s
      where you can create your own virus or make cures for viruses that come from
      outside.

      To make a virus or cure, you need a total of 4 symptoms you
      can purchase from the Black Market.

      If you check the computer in the
      Laboratory, you will be able to see all the informations you''ve gathered about
      each patient. <b>It matters!</b> Patients have higher or lower chance of infecting
      other patients depending on their personality traits and profession.

'
  topicExternalVirus:
    topicName: Unkown Virus
    topicBody: 'This is a special event that only happens if the player spends 10+
      days without creating their own virus.

      The Unkown Virus can only have
      symptoms already unlocked by the player.

      To cure it, you need to talk
      to patients, find what symptoms they have and then make the cure in the laboratory
      using the 4 correct symptoms.

      The longer the game progresses, the more
      dangerous this virus can become.

'
  topicSecretary:
    topicName: Fixed NPCs
    topicBody: '<b>Secretary</b> - She''s in the Clinic to assist you by giving information
      based on a few specific questions.

      <b>Dealer</b> - The man in the Black
      Market that sells symptoms. He only has 3 random symptoms available per day,
      so it''s advised you buy them when possible.

      <b>Spreader</b> - The man
      in the Black Market that spreads viruses. If you have your own virus with 4
      symptoms created and 100 coins, talk to the Spreader and he''ll infect a patient
      zero of your choice. '
  topicEndings:
    topicName: Game Endings
    topicBody: 'This game is supposed to have an emerging narrative, based on your
      actions. What you do matters, A LOT!

      There are 4 possible endings, but
      it''s your actions that define which one will be yours. '
  onBackPressed:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls:
      - m_Target: {fileID: 2065145611}
        m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: MainMenuController, Assembly-CSharp
        m_MethodName: OnReturnToTitleClicked
        m_Mode: 1
